<title>USA: Medusa Corp sees Q4 charge to redeem notes.</title>
<headline>Medusa Corp sees Q4 charge to redeem notes.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medusa Corp said on Thursday that it will incur a pre-tax extraordinary charge of up to $3.6 million, equal to $0.14 per diluted share, in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>The company said the charge covers the redemption of its entire $57.5 million issue of six percent convertible subordinated notes due 2003, which will be redeemed effective December 2 for 103.750 percent of principal, plus interest.</p>
<p>About $1.4 million of the pre-tax charge is unamortized note issuance cost, the company said.</p>
</text>
